1
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:49,799
<i>They're the ones I'd choose.</i>

2
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:56,139
About the other island,
looks like they were raided.

3
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,141
How?! Raided?!

4
00:00:58,725 --> 00:00:59,976
We’re not yet sure who did it.

5
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,312
<i>Some say there were armed men who did it.</i>

6
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:03,480
<i>Others say they were ordinary people.</i>

7
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,523
Others say they weren’t.

8
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,441
They weren’t people?

9
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:08,151
There were those who said…

10
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:10,070
it’s a bomb.

11
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:11,613
Really?

12
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,554
They're the ones I'd choose.

13
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:39,182
Then you've already made your decision.

14
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,936
So here's my suggestion
on what you can do.

15
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:48,066
These are just my suggestions.
Meaning you can follow them or not.

16
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:51,111
Because your situation
is extremely dangerous.

17
00:01:58,368 --> 00:01:59,744
What's your suggestion?

18
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:05,208
Wait for the right moment,
when you'll finish her off.

19
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:25,145
<i>She's often alone when it's time to sleep.</i>

20
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:58,094
Because if you fail,

21
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,430
you won't die an easy death.

22
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:04,976
She'll make sure your loved ones suffer

23
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,520
before she kills you.

24
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:12,609
Viktor!

25
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:19,198
Viktor!

26
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,244
No!

27
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,543
Sir Viktor! What are you doing?

28
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:33,421
You're going to drag me
into your death sentence!

29
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:36,549
I just got carried away.

30
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:53,441
Duh! You're right!

31
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:56,569
Come on.

32
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,196
My goodness!

33
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:00,823
Here's another suggestion.

34
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:05,036
La Morte Bianca loves drinking wine.

35
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:17,423
<i>Use that opportunity to poison her wine.</i>

36
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:23,429
<i>But the catch is,</i>
<i>she randomly invites people</i>

37
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:26,724
<i>to join her for wine night.</i>

38
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:28,643
Brusko.

39
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:06,723
Just throwing out ideas?

40
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:14,981
Because I want you to realize

41
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:18,192
that no matter how much we plan,

42
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:21,070
or how careful we are,

43
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:24,615
if we fail to kill La Morte Bianca,

44
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:26,993
we'll pay with our lives.

45
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,205
I know that!

46
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,052
We really need Chiara's help.

47
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:47,180
She has to bring down La Morte Bianca.

48
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:52,143
Whether G.A.G.O. helps her or not.

49
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:00,860
Is that it?

50
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,111
That's right.

51
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:04,072
And while we're doing that,

52
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:07,200
we need to keep up the act
of being loyal followers,

53
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:11,079
so La Morte Bianca won't suspect us.

54
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,414
Understood? Sir?

55
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:41,526
Want some company?

56
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:44,237
I don't need a jacket. It's not even cold.

57
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,079
Not cold?

58
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:54,831
Your cheeks are freezing.

59
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,542
Have you become that tough?

60
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:59,961
You can't even feel the cold?

61
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,677
There you go again, being so dramatic.

62
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:10,221
It's not winter here in the Philippines.

63
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:13,850
There's no way my cheeks are freezing.

64
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:20,898
I was just kidding!

65
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,275
You really can't take a joke.

66
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:24,318
Besides, that jacket isn't even mine.

67
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,112
I just found it in the living room.

68
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:28,448
How would I know whose it is?

69
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,782
Maybe it's Ben's.

70
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:34,871
It's like getting a hug from Ben!

71
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,748
Just kidding again! I'm joking.

72
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:39,083
It's actually mine.

73
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,376
- Come on. Wear it.
- No.

74
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,211
- No.
- No, thanks.

75
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:49,260
Why are you here?

76
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:51,596
Why aren't you inside with your girl?

77
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:55,975
I'm here because I want to talk to you.

78
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:03,691
Mikoy, haven't we already
talked about this?

79
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,156
Because I've had some realizations.

80
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,952
that made you put your time
with Chiara on hold

81
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,996
just to talk to me?

82
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:19,499
Nothing.

83
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:22,251
I've just been thinking carefully
about what you told me earlier.

84
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:27,882
Whether I let Chiara
go through with her plans because

85
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:29,383
I'm enabling her?

86
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:32,678
No. Not at all.

87
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:38,226
I realized I let Chiara do it
because I support her.

88
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:40,728
I believe in her plans.

89
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:44,482
Alex, I believe in the outcome.

90
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:50,404
To be honest, her life is on the line
with every move she makes.

91
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:54,116
She's risking everything just to help us.

92
00:08:55,451 --> 00:08:57,328
And while she's helping us,

93
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:01,624
I've noticed that she's trying
to rid herself of the things

94
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:03,876
that made her who she is.

95
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:07,046
Like what happened earlier, right?

96
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,967
She agreed to work together.

97
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:14,971
That's a big deal.

98
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:26,941
Besides, I won't
ask anything more for Chiara.

99
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:28,276
That wouldn't be fair to you.

100
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:31,737
You've already given
almost everything you could.

101
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,618
all the information we have right now,

102
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,580
Alex, we have it all because of Chiara.

103
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:44,917
Come to think of it,
she could've kept it all to herself.

104
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,128
But she didn't.

105
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:58,472
How long have you been there?

106
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,516
For a while.

107
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,893
I thought you two
would never finish talking.

108
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:05,896
Alex.

109
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:08,316
Tell me honestly.

110
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,571
Are you mad at me?

111
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:30,338
Chiara, like I told you,
I'm a professional.

112
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:33,799
I don't let my personal feelings
affect my work.

113
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:36,677
So whatever I said to you,

114
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:39,639
my frustrations, my rants…

115
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:47,229
So I hope you don't take it personally.

116
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:57,281
But once this is all over,

117
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:00,242
I hope we can be friends,

118
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:05,706
like we were at the bar,
when we first met.

119
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:10,252
I'd like that too.

120
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:27,645
That's more like it!

121
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,438
That's how it should be!

122
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:31,816
See? I told you.

123
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:34,819
We may be fools when it comes to love,

124
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:37,321
but when innocent lives are at stake,

125
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:38,614
we know better.

126
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:46,622
All right, Mikoy.

127
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:48,124
You two should head back inside.

128
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,543
Unless you want to keep
me company out here?

129
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:52,169
We're good.

130
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,421
It's getting cold anyway.

131
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:55,256
- We'll head in first.
- Okay.

132
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:25,911
You know, sweetheart, I'm so proud of you.

133
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,580
Why?

134
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:31,125
Because I want to be friends
with Agent Alex?

135
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,251
Not just that.

136
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:34,670
There are so many reasons.

137
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:42,720
And most of all,
for giving yourself a chance

138
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:45,306
to trust other people.

139
00:12:46,348 --> 00:12:48,767
I know that was a huge step
for you, sweetheart.

140
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:51,437
It wasn't an easy decision.

141
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,813
But you did it.

142
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:54,982
Wow!

143
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:57,276
You're not a bad mafia anymore,
sweetheart!

144
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:58,527
You're a good mafia now.

145
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:12,625
If you're not in the mafia anymore,
then what are you?

146
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,252
Mrs. Pinagpala.

147
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:18,589
Is that so? Wow!

148
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:20,382
You know,

149
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:24,970
I'm really excited for the bright future
that's waiting for us.

150
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:29,308
Me too.

151
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,236
Mikoy, hey!

152
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:43,239
Not there. Not there!

153
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:44,865
I'm here now!

154
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:48,285
Mikoy, stop! Mikoy, not there.

155
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:49,620
Ouch!

156
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,085
- Your mom's blue!
- Your mom's red!

157
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:57,545
Your dad's burgundy!

158
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:58,754
Give me that. It's mine.

159
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:00,756
Hey!

160
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:02,841
Kids, what's going on now?

161
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:04,718
Well, it's because…

162
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,762
They've been using it forever
and won't let me borrow it.

163
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:07,846
And you?

164
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,139
I wasn't even using it.

165
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,182
Wow!

166
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:12,476
Whatever! Figure it out yourselves!

167
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:14,520
- Let me see it!
- My goodness.

168
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,272
That's enough. Give it to me!

169
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:18,732
Your mom had a C-section.
Here, you wear this.

170
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:19,775
There, that's it.

171
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:30,077
- Hit him!
- What's going on here?

172
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:33,497
Stop! Come on!

173
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:36,917
Didn't I already set the rules
and assign your tasks?

174
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:39,169
We've been together here for days.

175
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,714
So why are you all
still arguing over the same things?

176
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:43,966
You, Dencio. Do you want me
to lock you up?

177
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,217
Why, ma'am? What would the charge be?

178
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:53,225
That's enough, all of you!

179
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:54,351
Stop it already!

180
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,394
Goodness!

181
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:56,645
Enough already.

182
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,898
Captain Pepe, take over for now.

183
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,900
Yes, ma'am. I'll handle it.

184
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:02,318
You heard what she said.

185
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:03,777
- Hey.
- I'll take care of it.

186
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:06,739
Hello, Bok. Good morning.

187
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,952
I just wanted to check in.

188
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,955
How are our grown-up babies
doing over there?

189
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:18,417
Do they need a little guidance from their…

190
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,294
Zaddie?

191
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,464
You know, if only my fist
could go through this phone,

192
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:24,757
I would've punched you already.

193
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,508
Don't provoke me right now.

194
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:27,635
I'm already so stressed.

195
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:29,553
Bok, you're unbelievable.

196
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,347
Can't you take a joke?

197
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,599
It's still early in the morning,
and you're already so worked up!

198
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,809
Smile! There you go!

199
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:39,897
<i>But actually, I'm not sure</i>
<i>this is good news.</i>

200
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:44,360
Because what I'm about to tell you
might just make you even angrier.

201
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:47,071
It's about 50-50.

202
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:48,739
What is it?

203
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:54,995
He's back in the Philippines.

204
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:56,956
He is?

205
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:59,416
So does that mean
Los Bandidos are in the Philippines?

206
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,210
Looks like it.

207
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:07,925
We need a boat!

208
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,135
Prepare the boat!

209
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,138
What's happening?

210
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:14,556
What's going on?

211
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,725
That's the third one in their family.

212
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:17,810
The third?

213
00:16:17,893 --> 00:16:19,895
That family is cursed.

214
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,230
Someone's always getting sick.

215
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:23,691
First, the father was hospitalized,

216
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,234
then the mother.

217
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:26,986
Cancer got her too.

218
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:29,279
Now it's the eldest child.

219
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:31,699
We wouldn't be surprised
if it's cancer too.

220
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:34,785
Maybe, it's hereditary.

221
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:36,328
We don't know.

222
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,789
They're the only family
around here with cancer.

223
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:42,918
Didn't they ever request an investigation
to find out why this keeps happening?

224
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:46,296
Maybe there's something wrong
with the island itself.

225
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,841
If there were something wrong
with the island,

226
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:51,301
why would they be the only ones affected?

227
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,887
Maybe their family really is cursed.

228
00:16:53,971 --> 00:16:57,808
Or maybe they brought something home
that wasn't meant to be there.

229
00:16:58,642 --> 00:17:03,439
So you all should
stay away from their house.

230
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:06,233
Even the people who visit
have been getting sick.

231
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:10,529
Anyway, I'm doing the laundry,
so I'll leave you now.

232
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:12,031
- All right.
- Okay.

233
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:21,248
It's 2026, and they still
believe in curses?

234
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:23,125
But you know,

235
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:26,587
I have a feeling there's something
inside their house

236
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:28,088
that they've overlooked,

237
00:17:28,172 --> 00:17:29,923
and it's what's making them sick.

238
00:17:32,551 --> 00:17:35,763
You know, mold can be
very dangerous to our health.

239
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:43,562
So, how do you think we can help them?

240
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:08,420
Wait, how?

241
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:09,546
How did you pull this off?

242
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,257
Did you have it delivered?

243
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,928
We're in a remote area.

244
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:19,640
Everything you see here

245
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:21,892
was prepared and cooked
by our safehouse mates.

246
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:24,937
And the reason they were arguing earlier
was to distract you,

247
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,855
so we could get everything ready.

248
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:29,233
How was our acting earlier?

249
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:32,111
Agent Alex, do you think
we could be actors now?

250
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:37,366
Hold on, hold on.

251
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:39,118
Don't think about the "how".

252
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:41,245
What's important is the "now".

253
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:42,538
Because it's your birthday.

254
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:43,914
- So, Happy Birthday, Alex!
- Yes.

255
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:46,542
- Happy Birthday!
- Your candle's about to melt.

256
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:51,547
I hate to say this, but…

257
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,340
it's not my birthday.

258
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:54,967
- Ha!
- He!

259
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:00,180
But thank you so much.

260
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:20,409
I wonder what Agent Alex wished for.

261
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,537
She said to enjoy the party,
so let's do that.

262
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:26,081
What are we waiting for? Let's eat.

263
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:27,291
Of course.

264
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,960
- All right, then.
- Here, here.

265
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,676
<i>We're so awful.</i>

266
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:41,054
<i>Who would be happy</i>
<i>to get a birthday surprise</i>

267
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:43,807
<i>when it isn't even their birthday?</i>

268
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:58,405
Alex. Are you crying?

269
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,116
Crying?

270
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:04,703
Because of this?

271
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:06,872
I just couldn't open it.

272
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:08,540
Oh? That's all?

273
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:11,001
Give it to me. I'll open it.

274
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:12,669
- It's okay, Mikoy. I've got it.
- I can do it.

275
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,838
- Mikoy. No, I can handle it.
- You can't even open it.

276
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:16,089
Come on, let me.

277
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:04,054
What are you looking at?

278
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:13,438
- Chiara.
- Sweetheart.

279
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:17,150
I'll take care of it.

280
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,420
I meant every word, Alex.

281
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:49,766
Hmm. But--

282
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:53,937
Chiara, come eat.

283
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,105
Come on.

284
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:16,585
Sofie.

285
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:25,052
After our outreach program,
and once we're back in Manila,

286
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:29,639
can I take you out to dinner?

287
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:35,062
My mom just came home from the States.

288
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:42,986
Are you listening to me?

289
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:47,783
I can't seem to find Angelito.

290
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:49,284
Do you know where he is?

291
00:22:54,831 --> 00:22:57,667
Miss, your nose is bleeding.

292
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:00,504
Are you okay?

293
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,546
Yes.

294
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:04,007
I'm just feeling a little dizzy.

295
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:07,260
Well, if you want, sis--

296
00:23:08,178 --> 00:23:09,971
Have you eaten yet?

297
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,306
Not yet.

298
00:23:11,389 --> 00:23:14,267
We've all been busy
taking care of my sister.

299
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:16,728
She had to be rushed to the hospital.

300
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,315
She's your sister?

301
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:23,568
What happened?

302
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:26,863
She's been in and out
of the hospital several times.

303
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:29,950
If it's okay, I'd rather
not talk about it right now.

304
00:23:30,784 --> 00:23:34,121
Too many things have been happening
to our family lately.

305
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,213
Oh.

306
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:45,590
Let me help you.

307
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,301
Wait…

308
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:02,399
Won't they be looking for you outside?

309
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:05,485
You're part of the outreach program.

310
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:07,362
I might be keeping you from your work.

311
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:11,449
We're here to help you.

312
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:13,827
Thank you.

313
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:20,709
How about Chiara?
Do you still suspect her?

314
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:22,752
I'm going to be honest with you, Mikoy.

315
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:26,339
I trust you, Mikoy, but not Chiara.

316
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:57,704
That's why I hope this fight ends soon,
so you can visit your father,

317
00:24:57,787 --> 00:25:00,874
and I can be with my family.
